embedding-3-small", "object": "list", "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 5987, "total_tokens": 5987}}, "input": {"input": ["# SAP BTP Community Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of the SAP BTP community, focusing on key components, their relationships, and significant updates. The information is relevant to the community's operations as of 2024.\n\n## Security Updates and Enhancements\n\nThe SAP BTP community has implemented several security updates and enhancements to strengthen platform security. These include the removal of weak client certificate chains, the deletion of TLS 1.2 Cipher-Block-Chaining (CBC) Ciphers, and the introduction of new security features. These updates aim to protect the community from potential security threats and ensure compliance with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (466, 3841), Date_Range ((2023, 10, 19), (2024, 02, 22))]\n\n## Component Updates and Deprecations\n\nThe SAP BTP community has introduced several component updates and deprecations to improve the overall user experience and ensure operational stability. These include the removal of SAP Java Buildpack 1, the introduction of new regions, and the enhancement of existing components. These updates aim to provide users with a more streamlined and efficient experience. [Data: Sources (1111, 2201), Date_Range ((2024, 04, 03), (2024, 09, 30))]\n\n## Cloud Connector and IP Addresses\n\nThe SAP BTP community has introduced several updates related to Cloud Connector and IP addresses. These include the addition of new IP addresses, the removal of deprecated IP addresses, and the introduction of new security features. These updates aim to ensure the community's compliance with regulatory requirements and provide users with a more secure experience. [Data: Sources (3383, 3842), Date_Range ((2023, 11, 02), (2024, 02, 22))]", "# SAP BTP Technology Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP BTP's key technology components, highlighting their relationships and significant updates as of 2024. The information is relevant to SAP BTP's operations and maintenance.\n\n## SAP BTP Security Updates\n\nSAP BTP has implemented several security updates to strengthen platform security, including the removal of weak client certificate chains and the deprecation of CBC ciphers. These changes aim to prevent potential security vulnerabilities and ensure the platform's integrity. Effective security measures not only prevent security breaches but also support the company's strategic decision-making processes and compliance with regulatory standards. [Data: Sources (466, 722), Date_Range ((2023, 11, 16), (2024, 02, 22))]\n\n## SAP BTP Technology Component Updates\n\nSAP BTP has released several updates to its technology components, including the SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry Runtime, and the Authorization and Trust Management Service. These updates aim to improve the platform's stability, scalability, and security, ensuring a seamless user experience and efficient operations. The updates also reflect SAP BTP's commitment to innovation and customer satisfaction. [Data: Sources (466, 722), Date_Range ((2023, 11, 02), (2024, 10, 15))]\n\n## SAP BTP Regional Updates\n\nSAP BTP has made several updates to its regional infrastructure, including the addition of new regions and the deprecation of old ones. These updates aim to improve the platform's availability, scalability, and performance, ensuring a seamless user experience and efficient operations. The updates also reflect SAP BTP's commitment to innovation and customer satisfaction. [Data: Sources (466, 722), Date_Range ((2023, 11, 02), (2025, 09, 19))]", "# SAP BTP and Kyma Runtime Overview as of 2023-2025\n\nThis report delves into SAP BTP and Kyma Runtime's key components, focusing on their interactions and updates within the organizational framework to uphold regulatory standards and manage financial risks effectively. The information is relevant to the company's operations around 2023-2025.\n\n## SAP BTP Security Updates\n\nSAP BTP has been updating its security measures to ensure the protection of its users' data. This includes the removal of deprecated cipher suites and the addition of new security features. The removal of the Ory Hydra component and APIRule in version v1alpha1 has been deprecated since Kyma 2.5, and its end of life is planned for Kyma 2.19. Migrate your APIRules to v1beta1. To do that, you must change the apiVersion field of your existing APIRule custom resources to gateway.kyma-project.io/v1beta1. Read the APIRule CR documentation to learn more about the specification of each version. [Data: Sources (4051, 4052, 4053), Date_Range ((2023, 09, 05), (2023, 10, 14))]\n\n## Kyma Runtime Updates\n\nKyma Runtime has been updating its features to improve its performance and security. This includes the addition of new logging options and the removal of deprecated components. The release of the Serverless module has been announced, and the Serverless custom resource API has been added. [Data: Sources (4140, 4056), Date_Range ((2023, 09, 28), (2023, 10, 14))]\n\n## SAP BTP and Kyma Runtime Interactions\n\nSAP BTP and Kyma Runtime have been interacting to improve their performance and security. This includes the addition of new features and the removal of deprecated components. The SAP BTP Operator module 1.0.0 has been released, and the SAP BTP service operator resources have been upgraded to version 0.5.3. [Data: Sources (3998), Date_Range ((2023, 10, 24), (2023, 10, 24))]", "# SAP BTP and Cloud Foundry Runtime Overview as of 2023-2024\n\nThis report delves into SAP BTP and Cloud Foundry Runtime's key components, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to uphold platform security and manage applications effectively. The information is relevant to the company's operations around 2023-2024.\n\n## Cloud Foundry Runtime Updates\n\nCloud Foundry has been updated from version 35.1.0 to 36.0.0, and then to 39.8.0, with various bug fixes and security enhancements. This update ensures that the platform remains secure and stable, supporting the company's applications and services effectively. [Data: Sources (3532, 3533), Date_Range ((2024, 02, 08), (2024, 04, 18))]\n\n## SAP BTP Service Operator Enhancements\n\nThe SAP BTP Service Operator has been enhanced to support custom formats for service binding secrets, allowing developers to model their service binding secrets according to their needs. This feature enables more flexibility and customization in service binding, supporting the company's application development and deployment processes. [Data: Sources (3105), Date_Range ((2024, 04, 08), (2024, 04, 18))]\n\n## Cloud Connector Updates\n\nThe Cloud Connector has been updated to version 2.16.1, with various bug fixes and security enhancements. This update ensures that the Cloud Connector remains secure and stable, supporting the company's applications and services effectively. [Data: Sources (3843), Date_Range ((2023, 10, 05), (2024, 01, 01))]", "# SAP Technology Overview as of 2024-10-02\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP's key technology components, highlighting their relationships and core attributes. The information is relevant to SAP's operations as of 2024-10-02.\n\n## SAP Build Process Automation Operational Scope\n\nSAP Build Process Automation plays a pivotal role in automating business processes. Its proactive approach helps safeguard SAP against potential operational pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective process automation not only prevents operational anomalies but also supports SAP's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (290, 2187), Date_Range ((2024, 10, 02), (2024, 10, 02))]\n\n## Cloud Identity Services and Continuous Integration & Delivery\n\nCloud Identity Services and Continuous Integration & Delivery are critical components of SAP's technology stack. They ensure seamless integration and delivery of SAP's products and services. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high standards of security and operational excellence. [Data: Sources (2183, 2184), Date_Range ((2024, 09, 25), (2024, 10, 02))]\n\n## SAP Task Center and SAP Build Process Automation\n\nSAP Task Center and SAP Build Process Automation are key components of SAP's technology stack. They enable efficient task management and process automation. Their collaboration ensures that risk mitigation strategies are legally sound and that compliance measures consider financial risks. [Data: Sources (2187, 2189), Date_Range ((2024, 10, 02), (2024, 10, 02))]", "# SAP Technology Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP's key technology components, highlighting their relationships and significant updates as of 2024. The information is relevant to SAP's technology operations and development.\n\n## SAP BTP Command Line Interface Updates\n\nThe SAP BTP Command Line Interface has undergone significant updates, including the deprecation of client versions 2.54 through 2.61 and the expansion of the btp CLI command autocompletion feature. These changes aim to improve user experience and ensure compatibility with the latest SAP BTP services. [Data: Sources (483, 123), Date_Range ((2024, 11, 26), (2024, 11, 28))]\n\n## Cloud Foundry Updates\n\nCloud Foundry has been updated from version 44.3.0 to 44.5.0, introducing new features and improvements. This update aims to enhance the overall performance and user experience of Cloud Foundry services. [Data: Source (3308), Date_Range ((2024, 11, 28), (2024, 11, 28))]\n\n## SAP BTP Cockpit Enhancements\n\nThe SAP BTP Cockpit has undergone several enhancements, including the addition of a new option to create subaccounts based on existing ones and the ability to export filtered usage and costs data. These changes aim to improve user experience and provide more flexibility in managing SAP BTP services. [Data: Sources (490, 3240), Date_Range ((2024, 06, 27), (2024, 06, 27))]", "# SAP Cloud Services Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP Cloud Services, highlighting key components, their relationships, and significant updates. The information is relevant to the company's operations around 2024.\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Operational Scope\n\nCloud Identity Services at SAP plays a pivotal role in providing identity and access management solutions. Their proactive approach, highlighted throughout 2024, helps safeguard SAP against potential security risks and ensures continuous compliance with evolving regulatory standards. Effective identity management not only prevents security breaches but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes and digital transformation initiatives. [Data: Sources (3364, 3365, 3366), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 12, 31))]\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Updates and Enhancements\n\nCloud Identity Services has undergone significant updates and enhancements in 2024, including the introduction of new features such as custom schemas, OpenID Connect, and authentication context class references. These updates have improved the overall user experience and enhanced the security of the platform. [Data: Sources (3302, 3303, 3304), Date_Range ((2024, 03, 12), (2024, 12, 31))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\n\nCollaboration between Cloud Identity Services and other SAP departments, such as Technology and Innovation, has been instrumental in integrating risk management with legal compliance strategies at SAP. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period has played a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (3369, 3370, 3371), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 12, 31))]", "# SAP Technology and Finance Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report delves into SAP's key departments focusing on technology and finance, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to uphold regulatory standards and manage financial risks effectively. The information is relevant to the company's operations around 2024.\n\n## SAP Technology Operational Scope\n\nThe SAP Technology Department plays a pivotal role in identifying, assessing, and mitigating financial risks. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2024, helps safeguard SAP against potential financial pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective risk management not only prevents financial anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (3431, 3432, 3433), Date_Range ((2024, 02, 02), (2024, 02, 18))]\n\n## SAP Finance and Accounting\n\nThe SAP Finance and Accounting Department ensures that all SAP's operations adhere to the legal standards set by regulatory bodies. Their focus on financial management and accounting, noted starting 2024, is crucial in maintaining SAP's reputation and operational legality, especially in managing complex financial transactions and accounting processes. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high legal standards and ethical practices. [Data: Source (3434), Date_Range ((2024, 02, 02), (2024, 02, 18))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\n\nCollaboration between the SAP Technology and Finance Departments, established in 2024, ensures that risk mitigation strategies are legally sound and that compliance measures consider financial risks. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating risk management with legal compliance strategies at SAP. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (3435, 3436), Date_Range ((2024, 02, 02), (2024, 02, 18))]", "# SAP Technology Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP's key technology components, highlighting their relationships and significant updates as of 2025. The information is relevant to SAP's technology operations and development processes.\n\n## Cloud Foundry Environment Updates\n\nThe Cloud Foundry environment has seen significant updates in 2025, including the addition of new regions, enhancements to the Create Node dialog, and improvements to the landscape action logs. These updates aim to simplify navigation, enhance automation, and provide more flexible table layouts for better data management. [Data: Sources (961, 962, 963), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 06), (2025, 08, 14))]\n\n## API Gateway Module Updates\n\nThe API Gateway module has undergone several updates in 2025, including the introduction of APIRule v2, the upgrade to version 3.0.2, and the update to version 3.1.3. These updates aim to provide more flexible access strategies, improve in-cluster connectivity, and enhance the overall API management experience. [Data: Sources (964, 965, 304), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 05), (2025, 08, 13))]\n\n## Data Space Integration Updates\n\nData Space Integration has seen several updates in 2025, including the introduction of new features such as Assignees Column, Software Version Update, and Contract References. These updates aim to provide more efficient data management, enhance collaboration, and improve overall data integration. [Data: Sources (966, 967, 1454), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 04), (2025, 02, 08))]", "# SAP BTP Technology Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP BTP's key technology components, highlighting their relationships and significant updates as of 2025. The information is relevant to SAP BTP's operations and development around this time.\n\n## Cloud Foundry Environment Updates\n\nThe Cloud Foundry environment has seen significant updates in 2025, including the release of version 51.5.0, which has improved the platform's stability and security. Additionally, the introduction of new features such as CAPTCHA protection and off-cycle upgrades has enhanced the user experience. These updates demonstrate SAP BTP's commitment to providing a secure and reliable platform for its users. [Data: Sources (96, 97), Date_Range ((2025, 09, 18), (2025, 09, 24))]\n\n## Kyma Runtime Updates\n\nThe Kyma Runtime has undergone several updates in 2025, including the release of version 1.44.0, which has improved the platform's logging, tracing, and metrics capabilities. Additionally, the introduction of new features such as configurable retention periods for subaccounts and support for additional signing algorithms has enhanced the user experience. These updates demonstrate SAP BTP's commitment to providing a secure and reliable platform for its users. [Data: Sources (352, 503), Date_Range ((2025, 07, 09), (2025, 08, 06))]\n\n## Decentralized Identity Verification Updates\n\nDecentralized Identity Verification has seen significant updates in 2025, including the introduction of new features such as revocation lists and support for additional signing algorithms. Additionally, the release of version 3.5 has improved the platform's security and stability. These updates demonstrate SAP BTP's commitment to providing a secure and reliable platform for its users. [Data: Sources (1713, 2651), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2025, 07, 03))]", "# SAP BTP Technology Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP BTP's key components, focusing on their operational scope, core attributes, connections, and noteworthy claims. The information is relevant to SAP BTP's operations as of 2024.\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Operational Scope\n\nCloud Identity Services at SAP BTP play a pivotal role in identifying, assessing, and mitigating risks. Their proactive approach helps safeguard SAP BTP against potential pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective risk management not only prevents financial anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (438, 415), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 03), (2024, 12, 03))]\n\n## Continuous Integration & Delivery Operational Scope\n\nContinuous Integration & Delivery at SAP BTP ensures that all operations adhere to the latest technological standards. Their focus on regional availability and new features is crucial in maintaining SAP BTP's reputation and operational stability, especially in managing complex projects and integrations. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high technological standards and innovative practices. [Data: Sources (894, 1729), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 13), (2024, 12, 16))]\n\n## Kyma Runtime Operational Scope\n\nKyma Runtime at SAP BTP plays a pivotal role in ensuring the company's adherence to technological standards and operational stability. Their proactive approach helps safeguard SAP BTP against potential pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective risk management not only prevents financial anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (2473, 1978), Date_Range ((2024, 07, 31), (2024, 10, 23))]", "# SAP Technology Overview as of 2023-11-01\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP's technology landscape as of 2023-11-01, highlighting key components, their relationships, and notable updates. The information is relevant to SAP's technology operations during this period.\n\n## ABAP Environment Updates\n\nThe ABAP Environment at SAP has undergone significant updates, with the XCO Library being extended to allow adding new worksheets to existing workbooks. This enhancement supports improved data management and analysis capabilities. The updates are part of SAP's efforts to maintain its ABAP Environment's competitiveness and relevance in the market. [Data: Sources (779, 780), Date_Range ((2023, 02, 16), (2023, 11, 01))]\n\n## Continuous Integration & Delivery Updates\n\nSAP's Continuous Integration & Delivery (CID) has introduced several updates, including the deprecation of native blue-green deployment, Node 14 and Node 16 build tool versions, and the introduction of new features such as batch inference configuration and document grounding capability. These updates aim to improve CID's efficiency, scalability, and user experience. [Data: Sources (3983, 3984, 2195), Date_Range ((2023, 10, 31), (2024, 09, 30))]\n\n## Kyma Runtime Updates\n\nKyma Runtime has received several updates, including the deprecation of serverless-registry-config Secret handling, the release of the API Gateway module, and the update to version 2.6.0. These updates aim to improve Kyma Runtime's performance, security, and user experience. [Data: Sources (3986, 2196), Date_Range ((2023, 10, 30), (2024, 09, 16))]", "# SAP Cloud Platform Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of the SAP Cloud Platform, focusing on its key components, their relationships, and significant updates. The information is relevant to the platform's operations as of 2025.\n\n## Cloud Foundry Environment Updates\n\nThe Cloud Foundry environment has undergone significant updates, including the addition of new regions and features. The SAP Forms service is now available in additional regions, and the Cloud Foundry environment has been updated to support new features and improvements. These updates aim to enhance the overall user experience and provide greater flexibility for users. [Data: Sources (758, 2641), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2025, 05, 29))]\n\n## Kyma Runtime Updates\n\nThe Kyma Runtime has received several updates, including the introduction of a new configurable parameter for additional worker node pools. This update enables users to introduce worker nodes optimized and reserved for their particular workload requirements. Additionally, the Kyma Runtime has been updated to support new features and improvements, including the addition of a new NATS module. [Data: Sources (3372, 3377), Date_Range ((2024, 02, 13), (2025, 05, 29))]\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Updates\n\nCloud Identity Services has undergone significant updates, including the introduction of central store-based provisioning and certificate renewal. These updates aim to enhance the overall user experience and provide greater flexibility for users. Additionally, Cloud Identity Services has been updated to support new features and improvements, including the addition of new API permission groups. [Data: Sources (1316, 1317), Date_Range ((2025, 02, 25), (2025, 05, 29))]", "# SAP Technology Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP's key technology components, highlighting their relationships and core attributes. The information is relevant to SAP's technology landscape as of 2024.\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Operational Scope\n\nCloud Identity Services at SAP plays a pivotal role in managing identities and access across various environments. Their proactive approach helps safeguard SAP against potential security risks and ensures continuous compliance with evolving regulatory standards. Effective identity management not only prevents security breaches but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (2669, 2668, 2667), Date_Range ((2024, 07, 02), (2024, 10, 09))]\n\n## SAP Task Center and Process Automation\n\nSAP Task Center and Process Automation are critical components of SAP's technology landscape, enabling efficient task management and process automation. Their integration with other SAP components, such as Cloud Identity Services, supports holistic governance and has been instrumental in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (2379, 2138), Date_Range ((2024, 07, 02), (2024, 10, 09))]\n\n## Cloud Integration and Edge Integration Cell\n\nCloud Integration and Edge Integration Cell are key components of SAP's technology landscape, enabling seamless integration with external services and supporting the company's digital transformation. Their integration with other SAP components, such as Cloud Identity Services, supports holistic governance and has been instrumental in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (331, 338), Date_Range ((2025, 08, 10), (2025, 08, 10))]", "# SAP Technology Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP's key technology components, highlighting their core attributes, connections, and noteworthy claims. The information is relevant to SAP's technology landscape as of 2024.\n\n## Cloud Foundry Environment\n\nCloud Foundry is a cloud platform provided by SAP, enabling developers to build, deploy, and manage applications. It supports a wide range of programming languages and frameworks, making it a versatile choice for various use cases. Cloud Foundry's scalability and flexibility make it an ideal platform for businesses looking to adopt cloud-native applications. [Data: Sources (295, 559, 372), Date_Range ((2024, 07, 18), (2024, 07, 18))]\n\n## SAP Build Process Automation\n\nSAP Build Process Automation is a low-code platform that enables businesses to automate and streamline processes. It provides a user-friendly interface for creating and managing workflows, making it an ideal choice for non-technical users. SAP Build Process Automation's integration with other SAP products and services enhances its capabilities, making it a powerful tool for process automation. [Data: Sources (295, 372, 372), Date_Range ((2023, 10, 13), (2023, 10, 13))]\n\n## Cloud Identity Services\n\nCloud Identity Services is a cloud-based identity and access management solution provided by SAP. It enables businesses to manage user identities, access, and permissions across multiple applications and systems. Cloud Identity Services' scalability and flexibility make it an ideal choice for large-scale enterprises with complex identity management needs. [Data: Sources (295, 372, 372), Date_Range ((2023, 10, 11), (2023, 10, 11))]", "# SAP BTP Technology Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP BTP's key technology components, highlighting their relationships and core attributes. The information is relevant to SAP BTP's operations as of 2024.\n\n## Cloud Foundry Updates and Enhancements\n\nCloud Foundry has been updated from version 32.3.0 to 32.11.0, introducing various enhancements and bug fixes. This update is part of SAP BTP's efforts to maintain a stable and secure platform. The update includes improvements to the platform's scalability, security, and performance, ensuring that SAP BTP can handle increased workloads and provide a seamless user experience. [Data: Sources (4039), Date_Range ((2023, 10, 19), (2023, 10, 19))]\n\n## Java Buildpack Updates and Enhancements\n\nThe Java Buildpack has been updated from version 1.77.0 to 1.78.0, introducing various enhancements and bug fixes. This update is part of SAP BTP's efforts to maintain a stable and secure platform. The update includes improvements to the platform's scalability, security, and performance, ensuring that SAP BTP can handle increased workloads and provide a seamless user experience. [Data: Sources (4040), Date_Range ((2023, 10, 03), (2023, 10, 19))]\n\n## SAPUI5 Distribution Updates and Enhancements\n\nSAPUI5 version 1.125 has been released for UI development and can now be consumed by SAP BTP services. This update is part of SAP BTP's efforts to maintain a stable and secure platform. The update includes improvements to the platform's scalability, security, and performance, ensuring that SAP BTP can handle increased workloads and provide a seamless user experience. [Data: Sources (2779), Date_Range ((2024, 06, 13), (2024, 06, 13))]"], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small"}}, "key": "embeddings_6636e212836fc3f0c4a08a44a7585d23864d0d68b67de9c13416fb721e2144f9_v2"}